HERE fits very well as an extra truck-intelligence layer

HERE currently supports truck routing using parameters such as gross/current weight, height, width, length, axle weight, axle groups, trailers and hazardous goods, and applies legal, physical and time-dependent truck restrictions. 

It even supports axle-group information such as:

single
tandem
triple
quad
quint

which is much closer to the kind of Alberta heavy-haul logic LeaseOS needs than ordinary consumer navigation. 

So we could use HERE in two ways:

MODE A — VALIDATOR

LeaseOS calculates route
        ↓
HERE independently calculates truck route
        ↓
Compare
        ↓
Investigate disagreements

or:

MODE B — ROUTE PROVIDER

LeaseOS sends:
truck + trailer + load configuration
        ↓
HERE generates commercial-truck route
        ↓
LeaseOS adds:
511
road bans
municipal rules
oilfield roads
company rules
        ↓
LeaseOS validates final route

I actually prefer supporting both.


