The Google part needs one correction

The concept you pasted is close, but I would not make this assumption:

> Calculate any arbitrary route ourselves and tell Google Maps to follow that exact polyline turn-for-turn.



Google's Navigation SDK can use Google-generated route tokens from Google's Routes APIs. Those let Navigation SDK try to preserve the planned route objectives, although Google says the navigation route can still vary because of changing road conditions. 

That's different from handing Google an arbitrary GraphHopper/HERE/LeaseOS polyline and saying:

FOLLOW THIS EXACTLY.
DO NOT RECALCULATE.

I would not depend on Google for that safety-critical guarantee.

Instead, separate rendering from routing

We absolutely can take our approved route geometry:

lat/lon
lat/lon
lat/lon
lat/lon
...

and draw that polyline over a Google map.

Google is then the visual basemap.

LeaseOS remains responsible for:

Turn instructions
Route adherence
Off-route detection
Truck restrictions
Rerouting
Warnings
511 state
Compliance

That's much safer.


